ero que verifiques el programa, que tu tengas el control completo ahora esta abierto\"* (`media_1793856121342_701977e6.png`).\n- **Success Criteria & Deliverables:**\n  1. Take full control of testing and verifying [`programa perfecto/PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe) (`v4.1`, source in [`programa perfecto/1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR/ProgramaPerfecto.cs`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR/ProgramaPerfecto.cs)) and [`V2/B866v2 Android 12/B866v2 Android 12/B866V2-FlashATV12 - Evoca.bat`](file:///C:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/V2/B866v2%20Android%2012/B866v2%20Android%2012/B866V2-FlashATV12%20-%20Evoca.bat) **100% externally without UART TTL**.\n  2. Diagnose why the box—which is currently displaying `fastbootd` on the TV screen—has not yet enumerated on the PC's USB bus (`PID_4EE7` / `PID_0D02`) and trigger/verify the external USB enumeration and the 4-step workflow (`1. Escanear la Memoria -> 2. Entrar en Modo Fastboot -> 3. Inyectar Firmware -> 4. Éxito Total`).\n- **Scope Boundaries & Mandatory Rules ([`REGLA_SIN_ABRIR_TORNILLOS_NO_TTL.md`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/.agents/rules/REGLA_SIN_ABRIR_TORNILLOS_NO_TTL.md)):**\n  - **Strictly 100% External (No UART TTL / No `SmarTTY` / Zero screws opened).**\n  - **Never mention or ask the user to click `Compilación` 7 times.**\n  - **Never flash `factory.img` (Widevine L1) or `cri_data.img` (MAC/Serial).**\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n1. **Reverse-Engineered ZTE's Recovery Binary ([`system_bin_recovery`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/experimento/11_VALIDACION_OTA_Y_FIRMWARE_ZTE/system_bin_recovery)) and [`init.recovery.amlogic.rc`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/experimento/11_VALIDACION_OTA_Y_FIRMWARE_ZTE/init.recovery.amlogic.rc):**\n   - Inspected strings and offsets in [`experimento/11_VALIDACION_OTA_Y_FIRMWARE_ZTE/system_bin_recovery`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/experimento/11_VALIDACION_OTA_Y_FIRMWARE_ZTE/system_bin_recovery):\n     - `Entering fastboot` (`0x31704`), `Set USB Status Success!` (`0x31737`), `SetUSBHost` (`0x34459`), `SetUSBDevice` (`0x37EFD`), `--fastboot` (`0x3E398`).\n   - Read [`experimento/14_MONITOREO_EN_VIVO_SMARTTY/INFORME_SESION_FASTBOOT_WATCHDOG_Y_SOLUCION.md`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/experimento/14_MONITOREO_EN_VIVO_SMARTTY/INFORME_SESION_FASTBOOT_WATCHDOG_Y_SOLUCION.md), [`experimento/13_CAPTURA_UART_TTL_SMARTTY/INFORME_FORENSE_UART_TTL_SMARTTY_REA.md`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/experimento/13_CAPTURA_UART_TTL_SMARTTY/INFORME_FORENSE_UART_TTL_SMARTTY_REA.md), and [`experimento/14_MONITOREO_EN_VIVO_SMARTTY/CAPTURA_DIRECTA_CONTROLADOR.log`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/experimento/14_MONITOREO_EN_VIVO_SMARTTY/CAPTURA_DIRECTA_CONTROLADOR.log).\n2. **Updated [`V2/B866v2 Android 12/B866v2 Android 12/B866V2-FlashATV12 - Evoca.bat`](file:///C:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/V2/B866v2%20Android%2012/B866v2%20Android%2012/B866V2-FlashATV12%20-%20Evoca.bat):**\n   - Added automatic `fastboot getvar is-userspace` detection so if the box connects in `fastbootd` (`PID_4EE7`), `Evoca.bat` automatically jumps to `U-Boot Fastboot` (`fastboot reboot bootloader`) without needing `SmarTTY` / TTL.\n   - Restored the exact EVOCA unlock command (`fastboot oem 'setenv lock 10100000;save` + `fastboot reboot bootloader`) while keeping `factory.img` and `cri_data.img` omitted and `:KEEP_ALIVE` (`fastboot getvar version`) active.\n3. **Updated and Recompiled [`programa perfecto/PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe) (`v4.1`):**\n   - Updated [`programa perfecto/1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR/ProgramaPerfecto.cs`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR/ProgramaPerfecto.cs) to remove intermediate sub-menus in `[PASO 3/4]`, include the raw EVOCA command `oem 'setenv lock 10100000;save`, automatically jump from `fastbootd` (`PID_4EE7`) to `U-Boot Fastboot` (`PID_0D02`), and keep the Anti-Watchdog `:KEEP_ALIVE` loop active.\n   - Compiled with `C:\\Windows\\Microsoft.NET\\Framework64\\v4.0.30319\\csc.exe` (`CSC ExitCode: 0`) and verified with `--check`.\n4. **Live Hardware & PnP Inspection (In Progress):**\n   - Verified `PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe v4.1` (`PID=20608`) is currently open on the user's screen and actively listening in `[PASO 2/4] ENTRANDO EN MODO FASTBOOT...` (`task-892` is tailing [`BITACORA_EN_VIVO_EXE.log`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/BITACORA_EN_VIVO_EXE.log)).\n   - Launched `task-911` to check `DEVPKEY_Device_LastArrivalDate` for all `VID_18D1`, `VID_19D2`, and `VID_1B8E` devices in Windows PnP.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n1. **Why the Box Does Not Enumerate on USB on its 1st Entry to `fastbootd` (and Why `SmarTTY` `\"reboot fastboot\"` Worked Before):**\n   - By default, ZTE's U-Boot (`env` partition) has `otg_device=0`. When the Linux kernel boots with `otg_device=0` on its `cmdline`, the `dwc_otg` driver prints `dwc_otg_driver_probe host only, not probe usb_otg!!!` and forces both USB ports into **Host-only mode** (`INFORME_FORENSE_UART_TTL_SMARTTY_REA.md` Hallazgo Crítico #3).\n   - When `/system/bin/recovery` enters `fastbootd` (`Entering fastboot`), it calls `SetUSBDevice` (`systemcontrol: [ubootenv] update value name [otg_device]: value [1] -> Save ubootenv to /dev/block/env succeed!`).\n   - **Crucial mechanism:** Even though `/system/bin/recovery` writes `otg_device=1` to `/dev/block/env` when entering `fastbootd`, the **currently running Linux kernel** was already booted with `otg_device=0`! Therefore, while the box sits in `fastbootd` the **first** time, the USB port does **not** enumerate on the PC until the box reboots **without** calling `SetUSBHost` (note: selecting `Reboot system now` calls `finish_recovery` -> `SetUSBHost`, which resets `otg_device=0`!).\n   - Previously, when the user typed `\"reboot fastboot\"` in `SmarTTY` while the screen was in `fastbootd`, it rebooted the kernel immediately (bypassing `SetUSBHost`) so U-Boot read `otg_device=1` from `/dev/block/env` and booted into `fastbootd` (`PID_4EE7`) with USB OTG Device mode enabled!\n   - **How to trigger that exact reboot 100% externally (No TTL) when the TV is in `fastbootd`:**\n     - Selecting **`Reboot to bootloader`** on the TV's `fastbootd` screen (or selecting **`Enter recovery`** -> **`Enter fastboot`**, or unplugging power while on the `fastbootd` screen so `SetUSBHost` never runs) reboots the box with `otg_device=1` intact in `/dev/block/env`, immediately activating the USB OTG port (`PID_0D02` or `PID_4EE7`) toward the PC!\n2. **Last PnP Timestamps for Box `Z41220090388172`:**\n   - `USB\\VID_18D1&PID_4EE7\\Z41220090388172`: Last connected `11/04/2026 01:10:28`\n   - `USB\\VID_18D1&PID_0D02\\Z41220090388172`: Last connected `11/04/2026 01:10:44`\n   - `USB\\VID_18D1&PID_4EE1\\Z41220090388172`: Last connected `11/04/2026 01:11:37`\n   - Currently (`23:24`), `Get-PnpDevice -PresentOnly` shows no external USB device from the box yet because the box is sitting on the 1st `fastbootd` screen where the kernel still has `otg_device=0` (until rebooted from `fastbootd` via `Reboot to bootloader` or power-cycle), OR the cable is on the non-OTG port.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Error 1: `ForEach-Object -Parallel` failed in Windows PowerShell 5.1 (`ParameterBindingException`):**\n  - *Root cause:* `-Parallel` on `ForEach-Object` is only in PowerShell 7+.\n  - *Fix:* Use C# `Parallel.For` or standard PowerShell loops.\n- **Error 2: `edit_file` failed on `ProgramaPerfecto.cs` on first attempt:**\n  - *Root cause:* `ProgramaPerfecto.cs` had already been updated to `1179` lines with `v4.1` auto-start logic.\n  - *Fix:* Read lines `600–960` of `ProgramaPerfecto.cs` and applied the exact `edit_file` target cleanly, then compiled with `csc.exe` (`ExitCode=0`).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Active Context\n- **Running Background Tasks:**\n  1. `5ecd42aa-1b9a-4dda-aec7-a32c9730884f/task-892` (`IsDaemon=true`): Monitoring [`programa perfecto/BITACORA_EN_VIVO_EXE.log`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/BITACORA_EN_VIVO_EXE.log) and watching for any `Evoca.bat` / `fastboot.exe` processes in real time.\n  2. `5ecd42aa-1b9a-4dda-aec7-a32c9730884f/task-911`: Checking `DEVPKEY_Device_LastArrivalDate` for all `VID_18D1`, `VID_19D2`, `VID_1B8E` PnP devices since Nov 1.\n- **Open Application on User's Desktop:**\n  - [`PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe) (`v4.1`, `PID=20608`) is open in Windows Terminal (as shown in user screenshot `media_1793856121342_701977e6.png`), already in `[PASO 2/4] ENTRANDO EN MODO FASTBOOT...` (`[*] ESCUCHANDO EN VIVO (Fastboot PID_0D02 / Fastbootd PID_4EE7 / WorldCup 48ms / ADB)...`).\n\n---\n\n### 6. Next Steps\n1. **Check `task-911` and `task-892` Results:**\n   - Call `manage_task` (`status`) on `task-911` and `task-892` to see if any new USB PnP arrival occurred.\n2. **Test All External Trigger Paths & Report Live Verification to the User:**\n   - Check if the box is reachable via Bluetooth (`BTHENUM\\DEV_9C2F4E99A11B` `Android TV` is present and `OK` in `Get-PnpDevice -PresentOnly`!), USB (`fastboot.exe`, `adnl.exe`, `update.exe`), or LAN (`arp -a`).\n   - Give the user a clear, immediate report of our live test results:\n     1. Confirm that [`PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe`](file:///c:/Users/andre/OneDrive/Desktop/xview/programa%20perfecto/PROGRAMA_PERFECTO_XVIEW_B866V2.exe) (`v4.1`, `PID=20608`) is running and actively scanning all 4 channels (`Fastboot PID_0D02`, `Fastbootd PID_4EE7`, `WorldCup VID_1B8E`, `ADB`), and that [`PASO 1/4`] passed 100% (`