 the current Linux kernel booted with a conflicting setting. Successfully activating the USB port requires a specific reboot path that preserves the `otg_device=1` setting. The desired external reboot bypasses the `SetUSBHost` call that resets this setting. Now the strategy focuses on ensuring that reboot preserves the correct OTG configuration.\n\n\n"}
